Gang Chen. MIT 2.58J Radiative Transfer, Spring 2006, graduate. [Course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-58j-radiative-transfer-spring-2006/) · [Professor and student notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-58j-radiative-transfer-spring-2006/pages/lecture-notes/).

Complete the available course progression on blackbody/surface exchange, electromagnetic material response, films/particles/gases, participating-media equations, discrete ordinates, spherical harmonics, Monte Carlo and near-field radiation. Work the available assignments and exams; distinguish thermal emission from coherent sources.

The public note table attaches files through lecture 23. Lectures 24–26 are listed without attached notes; do not treat their absence as completed reading. Student notes are credited to Tom Harris and used with permission. Compare dated examples with later primary research. OCW's general licence and separately credited components must be distinguished; everything remains externally referenced.

